1) Difference between SDLC and STLC process

SDLC (Software Development Life Cycle)- Focuses on developing software.
- Starts from requirement gathering and ends with maintenance.
- Performed by Business Analysts, Developers, Architects, etc.
- Goal is to build the product.
- Phases: Requirement Analysis -> Design -> Development -> Testing -> Deployment ->Maintenance.

STLC (Software Testing Life Cycle)- Focuses on testing software.- Starts from requirement analysis and ends with test closure.
- Performed by Testers and QA Engineers.
- Goal is to verify and validate the product.
- Phases: Requirement Analysis -> Test Planning -> Test Case Development -> Environment Setup -> Test Execution -> Defect Reporting -> Test Closure.

2) Who will do Unit Testing and What is the importance of Unit Testing? Explain about Quality Control

Unit Testing is performed by Developers.
  Importance of Unit Testing ;
- Finds defects at an early stage.
- Reduces debugging time.
- Improves code quality.
- Makes code maintenance easier.
- Increases developer confidence.
- Reduces overall testing cost.
- Ensures each function works correctly before integration.

Quality Control (QC)

-Quality Control (QC) is the process of identifying defects in a product and ensuring that the product
meets quality standards.
-QC Activities:- Unit Testing- Integration Testing- System Testing- Regression Testing- User Acceptance Testing (UAT)

QA vs QC

QA:
- Prevents defects- Process-oriented- Improves processes- Proactive approach.
QC:
- Finds defects- Product-oriented- Focuses on testing the product- Reactive approac.


